Slope tilt follows the ramp: hulls pitch when driving up and down hills.

The 0042 tilt table was 90 degrees off, so a hull driving straight up or
down a ramp got no pitch (only one crossing it tipped). Replace it with the
ground gradient of each TMP ramp type, measured on every multimd.mix map
(neighbour level minus ramp-cell level): 1-4 cardinal, 5-12 corner, 13-16
steep corner, 17-20 saddles (flat). Pick the cell by rounding (fx/fy cell
centres are integers; floor was half a cell late) and tip the turret along
its own facing.

